{"ruling":{"ruling":"FULL_REFUND","amount_sgd":5.00,"driver_compensation_sgd":null,"referrals":[],"confidence":0.95,"explanation":"Rider R-63263 booked TRP-06055 for a 05:30 pickup at Block 440, Pasir Ris Drive 6. Driver D-27956 was assigned at 05:28 and set off, but he never reached the pickup. The driver-device GPS trace (EV-GPS-06055, weight 1.0: 18 fixes at 30-second intervals, 100% coverage, no gaps, every fix reporting 4-8 m accuracy) shows him still working his way in and still roughly 2 km short of the pickup through its last fix at 05:37:00; the trip record (EV-TRIP-06055, weight 1.0) carries no arrival event at all and logs the rider's cancellation at 05:37:20. POL-NS-24 gives the rider the right to cancel at no charge where the driver has not arrived by the scheduled pickup time plus five minutes -- 05:35:00 on this record -- and refunds any fee charged in full; the record's own driver_deadline derivation returns arrived_by_deadline = false. The 5.00 SGD charged on EV-FARE-06055 (payment_status CHARGED, total_charged 5.00, refund_issued_sgd 0.00) is therefore returned in full.

The driver's points are answered. His contact obligation under POL-NS-23 was in fact met -- he messaged at 05:31:30 and 05:36:30 and placed an answered 35-second in-app call at 05:32:10, with contact_before_cancel.obligation_met = true -- but POL-NS-23 governs whether a no-show fee may be charged where the driver cancels, and it cannot cure a failure to arrive by the POL-NS-24 deadline. His argument that the record cannot establish the failure to arrive, so that POL-GEN-26 should escalate, does not hold: the GPS trace is complete and unimpaired and covers the whole deadline window (05:28:30-05:37:00), and its arrival check returns corroborated = false with nearest_fix = null, so the non-arrival is a finding the evidence carries, not a gap in it. The missing traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-06055-01 (weight 0.0, MISSING_ARTIFACT) carries no fact under POL-GEN-02(3), and no no-show clause admits a traffic excuse to the POL-NS-24 deadline.

Because the driver did attempt contact, the 5.00 SGD goodwill credit POL-NS-24 reserves for a driver who also failed to contact does not arise. No referral fires either: the fee charged matches the 5.00 SGD policy fee for POL-NS-22, and the rider profile does not carry the POL-NS-25 counter in a way that triggers a repeat no-show flag, so nothing is added to the refund. Both profiles carry fraud_flags = 0 and the contested amount of 5.00 SGD is below POL-GEN-22's 10.00 SGD threshold, so under POL-NS-26 this AI ruling is final. The rider is refunded the whole 5.00 SGD and the driver receives no compensation."},"discarded_claims":[]}
